Implement user story SKY-004-impl: Implement Express server with /health, /search, /cheapest endpoints and static dashboard

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts with Express app exporting named `app` separately from guarded `listen()`. Implement GET /health (always 200, never gated), GET /search (validates params, defaults adults to 1, returns FlightResult[] with count and searchedAt), GET /cheapest (returns cheapest or 404), GET / (serves src/public/index.html read from file at runtime). RAPIDAPI_KEY absence gates /search and /cheapest with 503. SkyscannerClient errors return 500 without crash. Create src/public/index.html as a styled dashboard with header, search form, and client-side JS. Update package.json with start/build scripts and supertest devDependency. Build must copy src/public/ to dist/public/.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports a named `app` (Express instance) separately from `listen()`; `listen()` is guarded by main-module detection (matching the tsup output format) so importing `app` in tests never binds a port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 with JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of whether RAPIDAPI_KEY is set or absent
- GET / returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type text/html; response body equals the runtime file contents of src/public/index.html (read via fs.readFileSync or equivalent), never a hardcoded inline string; this route is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- src/public/index.html is a styled single-page dashboard with: solid-color header bar (e.g. #1a73e8) with bold white title 'Skyscanner Dashboard' and subtitle; centered white card (max-width ~700px, rounded corners, border, padding) with 2-column grid search form (From/To IATA inputs row 1, Date/Adults inputs row 2, each with label); full-width colored search button; status area showing pink/red error banner, gray empty message, or success count; client-side JS submitting GET /search without page reload, disabling button during request, rendering results table inline
- GET /search with valid params (from, to, date required; adults optional, defaults to 1) returns HTTP 200 with { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: ISO-8601 } where count === flights.length and searchedAt is a distinct ISO-8601 timestamp per request; missing required param returns 400 { error: string }; non-numeric adults returns 400 { error: string }
- GET /cheapest with valid params returns HTTP 200 with the single cheapest FlightResult (price ≤ all others from same query); empty SkyscannerClient result → 404 { error: string }; missing required param → 400 { error: string }; adults defaults to 1 if absent
- When RAPIDAPI_KEY is absent at startup, /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / are unaffected. When SkyscannerClient throws, the server returns 500 { error: string } without crashing or emitting an unhandled promise rejection
- FlightResult is imported from the SKY-002 type export (not redeclared inline). package.json has 'start': 'node dist/server.js', a 'build' script producing dist/server.js, and the build copies src/public/ into dist/public/. supertest and @types/supertest are in devDependencies. `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0





